ard library\\012(`http.server`; no frameworks, no third-party packages, no JavaScript needed).\\012\\012Start it from the project root with `python app.py --port PORT` (a single `app.py` is fine; you\\012may add modules next to it). It listens on `127.0.0.1:PORT` and keeps its todos in memory.\\012\\012## Pages and forms\\012\\012- `GET /` returns an HTML page (`text/html`) that lists every todo and has a form\\012  `<form method=\"post\" action=\"/add\">` with a text input named `text`.\\012- Each todo is rendered as `<li data-id=\"ID\">TEXT</li>`, in creation order, where ID is its\\012  integer id (starting at 1) and TEXT is its text, HTML-escaped. A todo that is done has the\\012  class `done`: `<li data-id=\"ID\" class=\"done\">`. Each todo also has a small form to toggle it\\012  (`POST /toggle/ID`) and one to delete it (`POST /delete/ID`).\\012- `POST /add` (form field `text`) adds a todo and answers `303` with `Location: /`. Empty or\\012  whitespace-only text adds nothing (still `303`).\\012- `POST /toggle/ID` flips the todo between not done and done, and answers `303` to `/`;\\012  `POST /delete/ID` removes it, also `303`. An unknown ID is a `404`.\\012\\012## JSON API\\012\\012- `GET /api/todos` returns a JSON array of `{\"id\": 1, \"text\": \"...\", \"done\": false}`.\\012- `POST /api/todos` with a JSON body `{\"text\": \"...\"}` creates a todo and returns `201` with the\\012  new object. Missing, non-string, or blank text is a `400` with `{\"error\": \"...\"}`.\\012\\012Both ways of adding and changing todos work on the same list. Add tests and a short README.\n67232 67230 S          02:32 /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-darwin-arm64/vendor/aarch64-apple-darwin/bin/codex exec --json --color never --skip-git-repo-check --ephemeral --sandbox danger-full-access -C /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/codex-dev/todo-web/codex-1/ws/